  <title>Execute a command</title>

<p>Any input entered in the <app>Pano Terminal</app> to be executed is
  referred to as a <em>command</em>. You can run both command line and
  graphical user interface (GUI) programs from the terminal.</p>

  <steps>
<item><p>Type the command in the <app>Pano Terminal</app> prompt.</p></item>
<item><p>Press <key>Enter</key> to execute it.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>If you have a program that ends abruptly without any warning or error, you
  may want to run it in <app>Pano Terminal</app>. This will allow the program
  to output any error or debugging messages to the <app>Pano Terminal</app>
  window. This information can be helpful when filing a bug report.</p>

  <p>With <link xref="cmd-shell-integration">shell integration</link>, you can
  jump back to the prompts of earlier commands and copy their output.</p>

  <p>Read about the <link href="https://www.gnu.org/software/bash/manual/">Bash
  shell</link> for more information on what you can do in a terminal.</p>

